======================================================================
CKA Training Lab - Next Steps
======================================================================
Welcome to the CKA training environment!
Before starting your practice drills, complete the following initial steps:

* backup ~/.kube directory
* create the file ~/.bashrc-local
* add to it the following content:

source <(kubectl completion bash)
alias k=kubectl
complete -o default -F __start_kubectl k

export kdo="--dry-run=client -o yaml"
export know="--force --grace-period=0"

alias etcdctl="ETCDCTL_API=3 sudo etcdctl \
  --endpoints 127.0.0.1:2379 \
  --cert=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.crt \
  --key=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/server.key \
  --cacert=/etc/kubernetes/pki/etcd/ca.crt"

* to the end of ~/.bashrc, add the following: source ~/.bashrc-local

Exam Tip: Permitted web docs: https://kubernetes.io/docs/, https://helm.sh/docs/, https://gateway-api.sigs.k8s.io/. 
Fast terminal lookups: 'kubectl explain <resource>.<field>' .
(Note: Running 'make preprod-deploy' will automatically perform these setup steps and remove this reminder.)
